      {
        "id": 67694,
        "name": "Rabk",
        "username": "Rabk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-10-26T14:10:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Spiff wrote:</b><br><blockquote>&nbsp;<br><blockquote><strong>16. How does Dual Crowbars and Jack Handle react to one another if they are both in play?</strong>You would essentially deal all non-hero targets the damage twice.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote>\nI'm writing these up in the FAQ but got stuck on this one. &nbsp;How could you ever have both Dual Crowbars and Jack Handle in play at the same time? &nbsp;Whenever a Tool enters play, you have to return any other tools to your hand.\n</blockquote></div>\nFixed Point\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Sorry in advance for for the necro.</p>\n<p>I don't think this one works. Fixed Point makes all other cards indestructible, while playing a tool only returns any other tools already in play to your hand. The old tool leaves play, but it does not go to the trash and is this not actually destroyed as per RAW. [<em>Statement retracted. Please see my edit below.</em>]</p>\n<p>Fixed Point therefore shouldn't allow multiple tools to be on the board simultaneously. (It can do multiple styles, yes. That's a very handy little trick, particularly if someone can give you an extra card play or two while Fixed Point is in play.)</p>\n<p>[Edit to save confusion for those digging this topic up in the future: I didn't follow due diligence and double check the glossary definition for \"<span class=\"bbcode-i\"><span class=\"bbcode-b\">indestructible:</span> If a card is indestructible, it cannot be destroyed <span class=\"bbcode-b\">or removed from play</span>. If a target is indestructible, it stays in play even if it is reduced to 0 or fewer HP.</span> My argument was based off of the erroneous assumption that \"indestructible\" meant simply \"cannot be destroyed\" (i.e., put in the trash). Fixed Point <span class=\"bbcode-i\">does</span> in fact prevent tools from being returned to the hand. <span class=\"bbcode-i\">Exits stage left, hat firmly in hand.</span></p>",
        "post_number": 130,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:45:47.378Z",
